; An airline reservation system with no record of who holds a seat.  Ours, after McCarthy,
; "The Programming Language Elephant" (1979), section 5: "a passenger has a reservation if
; he has made one that has not been cancelled", and a request succeeds only if the flight
; wasn't full just before it.  The history is the chain of worlds; reserve and cancel are
; events that change nothing, and every answer is read from what happened.
start-world airline.
create Flight seats.
create Passenger.
make Flight F 2.
make Passenger P1. make Passenger P2. make Passenger P3.
action Passenger reserve.
action Passenger cancel.
qualify Flight booked (select all Passenger by which has-reservation = yes) size.
; a request at time T succeeded if the flight had room at T - 1
qualify Passenger reserved-at: T if (at time T it did reserve) and (at time (T - 1) F booked < F seats).
; a quantifier's body is one comparison, so the and needs parentheses to stay inside T's scope
qualify Passenger has-reservation if
  for some time T up to time do (it reserved-at: T = yes and
                                 not for some time U after T up to time do (at time U it did cancel)).
